 <td>PIVOT</td>\n                <td>₦1,650.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>FYNEFIELD</td>\n                <td>₦1,650.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DANGOTE</td>\n                <td>₦1,650.50</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>SIGMUND</td>\n                <td>₦1,675.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MATRIX WARRI</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MATRIX PH</td>\n                <td>₦1,675.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>PINNACLE</td>\n                <td>₦1,651.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>TMDK</td>\n                <td>₦1,640.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    FG Assures Dangote of Dollar Liquidity to Sustain Naira Fuel Sales – Sources\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Federal Government has assured the Dangote Petroleum Refinery that it will receive adequate foreign exchange to pay for crude oil purchases. The assurance, which was reportedly given during discussions held on Friday, comes as the implementation of the naira-for-crude initiative continues to face significant supply challenges.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/fg-assures-dangote-of-dollar-liquidity-to-sustain-naira-fuel-sales-sources\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Oil Prices Fall Over 5% as Trump Pauses Iran Strikes\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude was trading at $83.44 per barrel, down 5.11 per cent. West Texas Intermediate (WTI) crude fell 5.82 per cent to $79.74 per barrel. The sharp decline follows weeks of heightened volatility across the global oil market.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/oil-prices-fall-over-5-as-trump-pauses-iran-strikes\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Trump Says U.S. Halts Planned Iran Strike as Hormuz Deal Takes Shape\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    U.S. President Donald Trump said the United States has suspended a planned military strike against Iran. Trump said he agreed to cancel the planned attack after being informed that the outlines of a possible agreement had been reached. He said his decision to suspend military action was conditional on progress toward a final agreement.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/trump-says-us-halts-planned-iran-strike-as-hormuz-deal-takes-shape\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Dangote Refinery Receives 23 Crude Cargoes as Nigerian Grades Account for 70%\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Dangote Petroleum Refinery received 23 crude oil cargoes totaling about 2.04 million metric tonnes and 7.16 million barrels between July and early August 2026. Nigerian grades accounting for nearly 70% of scheduled deliveries, according to a vessel movement schedule reviewed by petroleumprice.ng.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/dangote-refinery-receives-23-crude-cargoes-as-nigerian-grades-account-for-70\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Saudi Oil Tankers Reroute Around Africa as Red Sea Risks Persist\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Saudi Arabia has begun redirecting some of its crude oil tanker movements away from the Bab el-Mandeb Strait. At least six empty tankers taking a longer route around Africa following renewed security concerns in the Red Sea. Routing around southern Africa is expected to extend the journey of a Very Large Crude Carrier (VLCC) by at least two weeks.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/saudi-oil-tankers-reroute-around-africa-as-red-sea-risks-persist\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
